---
title: Main-window close states (shell::Lifecycle, implemented, AD 20)
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  [*] --> Open
  Open --> Quiescing : window close requested by the close button or --close-after-secs, then HostControl begin_quiesce
  Quiescing --> Persisting : no request in flight and quiesced(), or 10 s bound
  Persisting --> ShuttingDown : view state saved, Engine begin_shutdown
  Persisting --> Exiting : no runtime (offline shell)
  ShuttingDown --> Exiting : Runtime shutdown finished (summary shown)
  Exiting --> Closed : ViewportCommand Close
  Closed --> [*]
  note right of ShuttingDown
    The window stays responsive and shows progress.
    Nothing keeps running in a tray or daemon.
    Quiescing is the seam where run controls (planned, DW-9)
    pause every active work root, in this build a no-op.
  end note
